 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1876, it rained raw meat on a Kentucky farm.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.711
  },
  {
   "text": "Mrs. Crouch was making soap outside. The sky was perfectly clear.",
   "s": 4.011,
   "e": 7.534
  },
  {
   "text": "Then red flakes started slapping the ground around her.",
   "s": 7.834,
   "e": 10.185
  },
  {
   "text": "Some were four inches wide. They covered a whole football field.",
   "s": 10.485,
   "e": 13.457
  },
  {
   "text": "So two brave men tasted it. Their verdict: mutton, maybe venison.",
   "s": 13.757,
   "e": 17.338
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it got worse: scientists tested it.",
   "s": 17.638,
   "e": 19.4
  },
  {
   "text": "The meat was lung tissue, most likely thrown up by vultures.",
   "s": 19.7,
   "e": 22.833
  },
  {
   "text": "Scared vultures vomit so they can fly away lighter.",
   "s": 23.133,
   "e": 25.724
  },
  {
   "text": "So the meat those men tasted? Vulture vomit.",
   "s": 26.024,
   "e": 28.374
  }
 ],
